WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:02.535
Detection logic depends on telemetry.

00:00:02.535 --> 00:00:06.110
An analytic can only evaluate behavior that the organization can observe,

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:10.000
and its reliability depends on stable fields, understandable semantics,

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.235
appropriate retention, and predictable delivery from the underlying sources.

00:00:13.235 --> 00:00:16.140
Detection planning should therefore begin with data requirements.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.560
Engineers identify the behavior to observe, determine which sources record it,

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.965
confirm the necessary fields, and test how normal and suspicious scenarios appear.

00:00:23.965 --> 00:00:27.460
This prevents rules from being designed around data that does not exist or cannot be

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:27.990
trusted.

00:00:27.990 --> 00:00:30.700
Telemetry context also affects detection quality.

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:35.000
Asset criticality, identity role, device state, vulnerability information,

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.302
and prior activity can help a detection distinguish routine behavior from meaningful risk.

00:00:39.302 --> 00:00:43.672
Poor context may create noise or leave analysts without enough information to triage an

00:00:43.672 --> 00:00:44.195
alert.

00:00:44.195 --> 00:00:46.000
Detection and telemetry teams need a feedback loop.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:50.265
When fields change, sources stop reporting, or analysts identify missing context,

00:00:50.265 --> 00:00:52.190
detections should be reviewed.

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:52.600
Likewise,

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:56.740
detection failures can reveal collection gaps that deserve engineering attention and

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.060
coverage investment.

00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.965
Testing should cover the data pipeline as well as the analytic rule.

00:00:59.965 --> 00:01:03.710
Teams can generate an approved test event, confirm that the source records it,

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:07.000
verify that collection and parsing preserve the expected fields,

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:10.000
and then check whether the detection produces useful context.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.950
This end-to-end method separates logic problems from telemetry failures and supports safer

00:01:13.950 --> 00:01:15.000
change management.
